  "question": {
    "html": "<p>Two masses <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"M\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"m\"></span> are connected by a string that runs without friction through a stationary tube. Mass <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"m\"></span> rotates at constant speed in a horizontal circle of radius 0.25 m. The weight of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"M\"></span> provides the centripetal force for the motion of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"m\"></span>. The time period for the rotation of m is 0.50 s.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>What is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{\\textit{mass of M}}{\\textit{mass of m}}\"></span>?</p>\n<p>[1]</p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\">1</li><li data-label=\"B\">2</li><li data-label=\"C\">4</li><li data-label=\"D\">8</li></ol>"
  },
